- op: discuss  # 7f53
  at: '2026-03-02T23:43:43Z'  # 7f53
  by: agent  # 7f53
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7f53
  clock: 4  # 7f53
  nonce: 7f53  # 7f53
  message: "Independent external bakeoff (March 2026, Jenkins/Kong/Vault) confirms and strengthens this invariant violation with concrete data.\n\nAnalyst used a custom \"reach3\" metric (3-hop BFS over calls edges, test-excluded) and found:\n- Jenkins: auto-selects MyViewsProperty (64 slice nodes but ZERO outgoing frontier calls — an island) over SetupWizard.doCreateAdminUser (57 nodes, rich connectivity, zero missing call targets)\n- Vault: auto-selects tools/stubmaker/main.go (reach3=24) and peripheral plugin CLIs (reach3=13) over the actual HTTP API surface (handleSysSealStatus etc.)\n- Kong: auto-selected Kong.init_worker is actually the best candidate (reach3=47) — one repo where it works\n\nThe analyst recommends: \"incorporating a lightweight reachability signal into entrypoint scoring — even a 1-hop or 2-hop internal call count — would meaningfully improve auto-slice quality.\" This aligns with the existing INV description but provides the clearest external evidence yet that the fix is high-leverage.\n\nThe analyst also showed that main_function and http_route kinds are favored by confidence, but confidence doesn't account for downstream reachability. Route nodes with routes_to edges (Vault's actual API surface) don't appear in top entrypoints because they're kind=route, not kind=main_function.\n\nSource: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/hypergumbo-v2.1.0-bakeoff-jenkins-kong-vault-20260302.md"  # 7f53
